       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily comes to 6 g/day, which is well above the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day. Many institutions cap it at 3 g/day. A single 2000 mg dose is also double the standard maximum single dose of 1000 mg. That puts the patient at risk of hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **1000 mg orally three times daily** (3 g/day), a common conservative regimen\n- **1000 mg orally four times daily** (4 g/day), the standard maximum\n- **650 mg orally every 6 hours** (2.6 g/day)\n\nTell me which one you want, or give me different parameters, and I'll enter it. Please also check the intended dose with your resident or attending. Make sure the patient isn't getting acetaminophen from other sources, such as combination products."
